{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 27, :comments ["<b>You shall not round, etc.</b> Regarding the rounding of the head He used plural language, and regarding the marring of the beard He used singular language — to say that one is included in the prohibition of ״לֹא תַקִּיף״ even though he is not included in the prohibition of ״לֹא תַשְׁחִית,״ such as one who does not yet have the growth of a beard — so that you should not say: since he is not included in ״לֹא תַשְׁחִית״ he is not included in ״לֹא תַקִּיף,״ in the manner that they expounded (Kiddushin 35b) regarding the case of women, who are not included in ״לֹא תַקִּיפוּ״ since they are not included in ״לֹא תַשְׁחִית.״ And if you will say: what did you see to include these and to exclude those? — I include the males, who are included in ״לֹא תַשְׁחִית״ when they grow up, and I exclude the women, for whom there is never any ״לֹא תַשְׁחִית״ at all."], :book :leviticus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:59:24.977543411Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}